 drop among large makers (cea-shipments-q2).\n- Voltaris's share of Caldrian transformer shipments fell from 31% to 27% in Q2 2026, with Tarnwell and imports gaining (cea-market-share).\n- Quarterly revenue was C$905M, C$960M, C$980M and C$890M from 2025Q3 to 2026Q2 (n2.d3). The trailing four quarters sum to about C$3.735B.\n- The shipments document says shipments typically trail orders by about two quarters. Voltaris's H1 2026 orders were up 11% y/y (n2.d2), which is a possible offset. That one is for n2 to assess.\n\n**Implied 2027 revenue**\n- C$4.2B is about 12% above the trailing-four-quarter revenue of C$3.735B. The 2026Q2 run-rate of C$890M is about C$3.56B annualized, so the gap to guidance there is about 18%.\n- Hitting C$4.2B needs about 12–18% growth. The industry is now shrinking, and Voltaris is losing share.\n- Flat share and flat industry volume would leave revenue near C$3.6–3.75B.\n- A further share slip toward 25–27%, with the industry flat to down a few percent, would put revenue around C$3.3–3.6B.\n- Guidance would need a strong order-driven recovery in volume or pricing. The orders-to-shipments lag could allow that, but I have no data here on pricing or the size of the backlog.\n\n**Conclusion**\nIndustry shipments and market share do not support C$4.2B. My central estimate is C$3.5–3.8B for 2027. The upside risk is the 11% rise in orders flowing into shipments, which n2 should test.\n\nI could not fetch industry or share forecasts for 2027, so these figures rest on the Q2 2026 data and simple extrapolation.","ttft_ms":3001,"type":"result","duration_ms":23274,"uuid":"c162be27-f7b7-4a9f-a367-2de4d443c1db","ttft_stream_ms":2053,"time_to_request_ms":111,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":18,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":9,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":1,"model_c